{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014yoQM83AJT6ho9G16wcPbo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"liquid lithium\" self-diffusion coefficient \"cm2/s\" Murday Cotts 1968 value melting point 7Li\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS\",\"url\":\"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225135828_Self-diffusion_coefficient_study_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"Computer Experiments on Self-diffusion Coefficients of Some Liquid Metals\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11669-021-00868-y\"},{\"title\":\"Towards atomistic simulations of the SEI in Li metal batteries\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s41313-026-00092-6\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"Abstract\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2011.13703v1\"},{\"title\":\"Charge Distribution and Lithium Oxide Stability Modeled by Reactive Force Field\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpca.5c03998\"},{\"title\":\"Determination of emulsion size distribution by NMR restricted diffusion measurement - Li - 1992 - AIChE Journal - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://aiche.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/aic.690381019\"},{\"title\":\"Diffusion of Lithium Ions in Lithium-Argyrodite Solid-State Electrolytes from Equilibrium and Nonequilibrium Molecular Dynamics Simulations\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.02971\"}]\n\nThe 1968 Murday and Cotts paper reports the value you're looking for. It measured the self-diffusion of ⁷Li in liquid lithium by NMR, and it gives a value at the melting point of 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10⁻⁵ cm²/s (D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10^-5 cm^2/sec and (T/D)(dD/dT) = 2.8 ± 0.3, per the ADS abstract). A second source repeats the same value and cites the 1968 paper for it (6.8 ± 0.3 × 10 -5 cm 2 s −1). Their Arrhenius-type fit is D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10⁻³ exp[−(2300 ± 300 cal)/RT] cm²/s (D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10^-3 exp [ - (2300 ± 300cal) / RT]cm^2 / sec).\n\nThe melting point itself isn't stated in these results. One later paper models liquid lithium at T=454K, which is about 181 °C and matches lithium's known melting point, but that is a secondary source, so verify it against the original paper.\n\nThe results also say the paper compares its data with the Cohen–Turnbull free-volume model and the Ascarelli–Paskin dense-gas model (Results are compared with the Cohen-Turnbull free-volume model and the Ascarelli-Paskin dense-gas model for liquid diffusion.). The DOI is 10.1063/1.1668160 (J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938, 1968).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60e5bae0-74f3-4dab-b4d3-7504b260a251","uuid":"f5199738-be0f-4b03-b21a-2a8ae49cdb86","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:56:25.281Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"liquid lithium\" self-diffusion coefficient \"cm2/s\" Murday Cotts 1968 value melting point 7Li","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013Wtp9BG7wChMaDvSMVTien","content":[{"title":"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS","url":"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225135828_Self-diffusion_coefficient_study_of_liquid_lithium"},{"title":"Computer Experiments on Self-diffusion Coefficients of Some Liquid Metals","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11669-021-00868-y"},{"title":"Towards atomistic simulations of the SEI in Li metal batteries","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s41313-026-00092-6"},{"title":"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.res